Third-party material in apaar-register.mp4 and its source

Software used to make the film
- Lemo-Opuscar render tools (core/lib.js, core/render/*, core/audio/sfx.py): MIT licence, https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar.
  The Living Screencast engine structure (timeline, actor, cursor, camera) and the watercolour brush-stroke model were studied and re-written for this film.
- Playwright / Chromium: Apache-2.0 (screen DOM capture and rendering). FFmpeg: LGPL/GPL (encode). numpy, scipy, soundfile, soxr: BSD.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1, self-hosted in fonts/)
- Atkinson Hyperlegible (Braille Institute), IBM Plex Mono (IBM).

Voice
- Narration generated with Chatterbox TTS (Resemble AI, MIT licence). Chatterbox adds an imperceptible "Perth" watermark to generated audio; it was left in place.
- Speech-to-text check and word timings: faster-whisper with the Whisper base.en model (MIT).

Music and sound effects
- Original, synthesized in sound.py (felt piano, kalimba, upright bass and brushed percussion models). No samples, no third-party recordings.

Pictures
- The interface is the project's own application (this repository), redrawn from live DOM snapshots of a running instance with synthetic data.
- The mascot (a hand-painted admission slip) and every painted scene are original and drawn in code (mascot.js, paint.js). No external images.

The user is responsible for the materials they add to the film.
